.TH RELEASE 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
release \- Release a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B release
.I world
.br
.BI release "width point"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Release a region: unload its modules and delete its region row. The release is
reported back when done.
.PP
With a lone world number (0\-65535) that world is released, as before. With a
width and point the width\-wide ancestor of the point is released \-\- the same
point forms \fBgrant\fP takes (\fBhere\fP, \fBworld\fP \fIN\fP, \fBcosmos\fP, or
coordinates). A lone number stays a world, so always name the point, even for a
planet width.
.PP
Only the exact owner may release. The cosmos itself cannot be released: deleting
it would leave nothing ruling anything, so hand it over with \fBgrant\fP instead.
Unloading is best effort: one
stuck module is reported but does not veto the release of the rest, and the
row is deleted regardless, so nothing unloaded here comes back on the next
boot. The region entry itself stays behind, inert: a later \fBplanet\fP with
the same number reuses it.
.PP
Releasing is the counterpart of claiming, not of banning: it dissolves the
region's code and record, where \fBban\fP only refuses entry to one player.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR planet,planets,grant,loadmod,unloadmod (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
